[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2334801312","pull_request_review_id":3203322463,"id":2334801312,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6LKj2g","diff_hunk":"@@ -55,6 +160,11 @@ Error ZIPPacker::close() {\n \treturn err;\n }\n \n+Vector<uint8_t> ZIPPacker::get_buffer() const {\n+\tERR_FAIL_COND_V_MSG(zf, PackedByteArray(), \"ZIPPacker is still open. Call close() before retrieving the buffer.\");","path":"modules/zip/zip_packer.cpp","commit_id":"67d590c4ce4e735d97a4f6957d317ddda8b08383","original_commit_id":"67d590c4ce4e735d97a4f6957d317ddda8b08383","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`close` + `get_buffer` feels a bit overcomplicated. Calling `get_buffer` multiple times after closing is usually unneeded, so it might be better to have a single `finish`/`flush` method that will close the file and return data vector.","created_at":"2025-09-09T21:03:22Z","updated_at":"2025-09-09T21:14:51Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110341#discussion_r2334801312","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110341","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2334801312"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110341#discussion_r2334801312"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110341"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2334801312/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":164,"original_line":164,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":130,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2335211866","pull_request_review_id":3203940380,"id":2335211866,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6LMIFa","diff_hunk":"@@ -55,6 +160,11 @@ Error ZIPPacker::close() {\n \treturn err;\n }\n \n+Vector<uint8_t> ZIPPacker::get_buffer() const {\n+\tERR_FAIL_COND_V_MSG(zf, PackedByteArray(), \"ZIPPacker is still open. Call close() before retrieving the buffer.\");","path":"modules/zip/zip_packer.cpp","commit_id":"67d590c4ce4e735d97a4f6957d317ddda8b08383","original_commit_id":"67d590c4ce4e735d97a4f6957d317ddda8b08383","user":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It's similar to handling a physical file. The content should only be read after calling `close()`, otherwise it's a corrupted archive. But `flush()` won't work because it's the `close()` method that writes the required data block at the end of the file.\r\n\r\nAdding `finish()` as `close + return buffer` is counterintuitive to me, as now I have two seemingly unrelated ways to close a file: Should I call `close()` after `finish()`, or the reverse? And the answer is to call `finish()` only. If `finish()` is called after `open()`, it appears to be identical to `close()`, which feels confusing.\r\n\r\nI believe having a dedicated `get_buffer()` method is much simpler and clearer.\r\n\r\n> Calling `get_buffer` multiple times after closing is usually unneeded\r\n\r\nBeing able to be called multiple times is a side-effect rather than a design goal.","created_at":"2025-09-10T01:01:46Z","updated_at":"2025-09-10T01:01:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110341#discussion_r2335211866","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110341","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2335211866"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110341#discussion_r2335211866"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110341"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2335211866/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":164,"original_line":164,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2334801312,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":130,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"}]